      "matchText": "Toyura",
      "term": "Toyura",
      "definition": "A short-lived Yamato palace site in the Asuka basin where Empress Suiko held court early in her reign. Like other early Japanese capitals, it was a modest wooden complex meant to be abandoned and rebuilt with each new sovereign."
    },
    {
      "matchText": "Oharida",
      "term": "Oharida",
      "definition": "Empress Suiko's later palace in the Asuka basin, a few miles from the Toyura site. It was one of the impermanent court seats the Yamato sovereigns relocated reign by reign before Japan adopted fixed Chinese-style capitals."
    },
    {
      "matchText": "Kondo",
      "term": "Kondo",
      "definition": "The main worship hall (the “golden hall”) of a Japanese Buddhist temple, housing its principal images — the architectural heart of monasteries like Hōryū-ji."
    },
