      "matchText": "Daisojo",
      "term": "Daisojo",
      "definition": "The \"Grand Priest\" (大僧正), the highest rank in the Nara state's ladder of officially appointed Buddhist clergy. Emperor Shomu created it for the popular monk Gyoki, formally honoring the man the court had once persecuted."
    },
    {
      "matchText": "Kondo",
      "term": "Kondo",
      "definition": "The \"golden hall,\" the central image-hall of a Japanese Buddhist temple complex, where the principal Buddha statue is enshrined. Toshodai-ji's Kondo is the finest surviving example of Tang-influenced temple architecture in Japan."
    },
